From: mho22 <yannick@capsules.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] Answer the shell's IPC with fuzzel, swaylock, swaybg, Waybar and mako

Omarchy 4 runs one QuickShell process for its menu, pickers, lock,
background and notifications, and every script reaches it through
bin/omarchy-shell. Kandelo ships sway without QuickShell, so
omarchy-shell answers each call the in-scope scripts make with a sway
tool, and fails like QuickShell's IPC for any other call. A theme
switch sends Waybar SIGUSR2, which makes it read its style again.

omarchy-menu-fuzzel draws default/omarchy/omarchy-menu.jsonc and the
user's extension file one level at a time with fuzzel --dmenu. The
menu keeps the entries whose programs Kandelo ships. Every fuzzel call
passes the row count omarchy-menu-lines reads from sway, so the card
stays clear of the bar and the outer gaps like the shell's menu does.
The image picker lists each image by the label the shell's picker
draws: the file name without its extension, in title case.

omarchy-menu-select builds its payload with jq instead of perl, and
omarchy-menu-images lists the images themselves when vipsthumbnail is
missing. Kandelo ships neither perl in this image nor libvips. Without
libvips each image is its own final row, not a pending thumbnail, so
the picker still caches its rows and a later open skips the per-image
stat, awk and md5sum calls.

A menu action can start hundreds of processes before its picker
shows, and each process start costs tens of milliseconds on Kandelo,
so omarchy-menu-fuzzel shows a mako notification "Loading <entry>…"
until omarchy-shell opens the picker or the action ends. A menu level
shows "Loading <level>…" while it starts the processes that build its
rows, and dismisses it as fuzzel starts. omarchy-shell
answers image-selector preload with success: fuzzel keeps no picker
between opens, so the rows the caller cached are the whole preload.
omarchy-theme-switcher rebuilds its previews under a lock: the session
preloads it at start, and a Theme pick made during that preload would
otherwise empty the directory the preload fills.

omarchy-menu-images waits on its cache locks with flock and no -w
timeout. Kandelo's flock is busybox's applet, which has no -w option.

omarchy-shell, omarchy-menu and omarchy-menu-fuzzel take --check: it
runs nothing and exits 0 only when the call has an answer, so a key
binding is made only for a call that does something.

